+<body>
+  <a class="skip-link" href="#content">Skip to content</a>
+  <header class="site-header"><div class="header-inner"><a class="logo" href="/bidetfit/"><span class="logo-mark" aria-hidden="true">B</span>BidetFit</a><nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/bidetfit/">Home</a><a class="nav-primary" href="/bidetfit/fit-checker.html">Fit checker</a><a href="/bidetfit/how-to-measure.html">Measure</a><a href="/bidetfit/disclosure.html">Disclosure</a></nav></div></header>
+  <main id="content">
+    <section class="page-hero"><div class="narrow">
+      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/bidetfit/">BidetFit</a><span>/</span><span>Answers</span></div>
+      <span class="eyebrow">Fit question</span>
+      <h1>Will an elongated toilet take a round bidet seat?</h1>
+      <p class="lede">Usually no. Manufacturer fit guidance treats round and elongated as different seat geometries. Measure the bowl before buying.</p>
+    </div></section>
+    <article class="section"><div class="narrow prose">
+      <h2>Short answer</h2>
+      <p>Choose a seat shape that matches the toilet bowl. An elongated bowl generally needs an elongated seat; a round bowl generally needs a round seat. Mixing shapes is a common return cause and is not something BidetFit recommends as a workaround.</p>
+      <h2>What manufacturers say</h2>
+      <ul>
+        <li><a href="https://biobidet.com/pages/compatibility" rel="noreferrer">Bio Bidet compatibility guide</a> — start with toilet/seat compatibility checks rather than guessing from a photograph.</li>
+        <li><a href="https://biobidet.com/blogs/news/will-a-bidet-fit-my-toilet" rel="noreferrer">Bio Bidet “Will a bidet fit my toilet?”</a> — emphasizes measuring and confirming shape/clearance before purchase.</li>
+        <li><a href="https://bidetking.com/pages/bidet-toilet-seats-buyer-guide" rel="noreferrer">BidetKing electronic seat buyer/fitment guidance</a> — seat dimensions and bowl type remain first-order filters.</li>
+      </ul>
+      <p>Source pages were listed in BidetFit research on 2026-08-25 and re-checked for this answer on 2026-09-13. Re-read the live manufacturer page before acting; models change.</p>
+      <h2>What to measure</h2>
+      <ol>
+        <li>Bowl shape: round vs elongated vs unusual.</li>
+        <li>Bolt spacing and rear flat clearance for the seat housing.</li>
+        <li>Whether the seat overhangs or leaves gaps after mounting.</li>
+      </ol>
+      <div class="callout"><strong>No affiliate commission is claimed here.</strong> BidetFit has not activated approved affiliate links for this answer. See <a href="../disclosure.html">disclosure</a>.</div>
+      <div class="button-row"><a class="button" href="../fit-checker.html">Run the fit checker</a><a class="button secondary" href="../round-vs-elongated.html">Round vs elongated overview</a></div>
+    </div></article>
+  </main>
+  <footer class="site-footer"><div class="shell footer-grid"><div><a class="logo" href="/bidetfit/"><span class="logo-mark" aria-hidden="true">B</span>BidetFit</a><p class="small">Manufacturer requirements are reported as manufacturer requirements.</p></div><div class="footer-links"><a href="../about.html">Method</a><a href="../disclosure.html">Disclosure</a><a href="../privacy.html">Privacy</a></div></div></footer>
